# detection_filter with unique_on, in the format of flow.cases: the window
# counts each port once, and alerts once more distinct ports than its count
# have been seen. make-flow-verdicts.py unique sends them to Suricata.

scenario a filter on unique source ports counts each client port once
> detection_filter:track by_dst, count 2, seconds 10, unique_on src_port; content:"UNIQ";
  0 > "UNIQ"
  1 > "UNIQ"
  2 > c1 "UNIQ"
  3 > c1 "UNIQ"
  4 > c2 "UNIQ"
  5 > c2 "UNIQ"
  6 > c3 "UNIQ"
  7 > "UNIQ"
  20 > c4 "UNIQ"
  21 > c5 "UNIQ"
  22 > c6 "UNIQ"

scenario a filter on unique destination ports counts the client ports a server answers
< detection_filter:track by_src, count 1, seconds 10, unique_on dst_port; content:"BACK";
  0 < "BACK"
  1 < "BACK"
  2 < c1 "BACK"
  3 < c1 "BACK"
  4 < c2 "BACK"

scenario a filter without unique_on still counts every match
> detection_filter:track by_dst, count 2, seconds 10; content:"PLAIN";
  0 > "PLAIN"
  1 > "PLAIN"
  2 > "PLAIN"
